NEAR Protocol opens its doors to Pearl, a coin mined with AI math

@NEARProtocol has added $PEARL to @near_intents and the near.​com app. Users can swap into PEARL from any supported chain and pay others with it; swaps are confidential by default, and wallets and apps on the NEAR Intents 1Click API can now offer PEARL swaps too.

Pearl is a separate Layer-1 blockchain from @prlnet, live since late April 2026. Its miners run the matrix math behind AI models on GPUs, and that same work secures the chain and issues new coins, capped at 2.1 billion.

Pearl keeps Bitcoin's SoV and swaps the work for AI math, where a GPU could serve a customer and secure the chain at the same time.

@minnus and I spent the last few weeks digging in. The design works, the economics aren't there yet, and the FP8 upgrade is the test.

If it passes, Pearl is the first PoW coin where the mining is worth something on its own

NEWS: Anchorage Digital Bank and Anchorage Digital Singapore now support native custody for Pearl ($PEARL), built by @prlnet.

Deposits, withdrawals, and wallet addresses are now live for clients.

@Anchorage https://t.co/VoNsYoBywP

Proof-of-Useful-Work proposes that the same GPU computation used for AI workloads can also secure a blockchain network.

But that immediately triggers an economic objection - if miners are already getting paid for running AI jobs, does the security of the network collapse?

@PassRafael breaks it down and shows why this critique doesn’t hold up. Worth watching 👇
